<# Fig / svg border kwarg form (#250) #>

These exercise the `border=true|false` kwarg on `<fig>` and `<svg>` — the form
`<frame>` / `<aside>` already honored via #186, but which `<fig>` / `<svg>`
formerly ignored (they read only `+border` / `-border`). Both default border OFF;
the kwarg now toggles it, via the shared `readFrameableBorder` helper.

<fig src=chart.png border=true | A figure with border=true — framed.>

<fig src=chart.png border="false" | A figure with quoted border="false" — unframed.>

<fig src=chart.png | A figure with no border kwarg — unframed (the fig default).>

<fig src=chart.png +border | A figure with +border — framed (the boolean form, unchanged).>

<svg border=true | <rect width="20" height="20" fill="teal" />>

<svg border=false | <rect width="20" height="20" fill="teal" />>
